\section{Subsystem Coupling and Data Dependencies}

The BAAC-SE v1.0 architecture is designed so that each subsystem provides
cryptographically authenticated outputs that serve as inputs to the next stage.
This ensures that no unverified or corrupted data can propagate through the
pipeline.

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Telemetry $\rightarrow$ CKKS:}  
    Raw astrophysical vectors are encoded into CKKS plaintext polynomials.

    \item \textbf{CKKS $\rightarrow$ Residual Witness:}  
    Decrypted plaintexts are compared against ideal reference models to produce
    bounded-error residual coefficients.

    \item \textbf{Witness $\rightarrow$ Groth16:}  
    Residual coefficients and bit-decomposition arrays form the private witness
    vector for R1CS constraints.

    \item \textbf{Groth16 $\rightarrow$ Actuation:}  
    Only verified proofs permit torque tensor dispatch.

    \item \textbf{Actuation $\rightarrow$ Audit Ledger:}  
    Every verified actuation epoch is committed to the Merkle tree and exported
    via ML-KEM.
\end{itemize}

